{"id": "EUVD-2026-86807", "enisaUuid": "40052c4e-290c-357b-a0ce-c281ee54f084", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: stmmac: fix TX descriptor availability check for TSO traffic\n\nstmmac_tso_xmit() estimates the number of free TX descriptors required by\na TSO skb as:\n\n\t(skb->len - proto_hdr_len) / TSO_MAX_BUFF_SIZE + 1\n\nwhich assumes the payload is split into TSO_MAX_BUFF_SIZE chunks. This\nunderestimates the descriptors actually consumed by stmmac_tso_allocator(),\nsince each fragment is mapped individually and so it needs at least one\ndescriptor regardless of its size. Moreover, one descriptor is used for\nthe L2/L3/L4 headers and, when the MSS changes, one more is consumed for\nthe MSS context descriptor.\nFor a highly fragmented TSO skb the check can therefore pass even when the\nring has too few free slots. stmmac_tso_allocator() then writes past the\navailable descriptors, overwriting descriptors still owned by the DMA\nengine, corrupting the TX ring.\nAdd stmmac_tso_get_num_desc() to compute the exact number of descriptors\nneeded for the header, the linear payload and each fragment, plus the MSS\ncontext descriptor when required, and use it in the availability check.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:49", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/09c30547da2c45bb79f7d3adffc860af332c2d42", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ffa6d2481bc1c87f822ecd626561484e4ee24cef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c28175220f808c867d5618de8ecc6dbcc815c773", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/65820fc743eae322f7f94f6a64d07861211d4b21", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e38d732ec67a5b1f9a56e6c73add480c4b6030a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97953", "GHSA-4j3p-7h59-gp38"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.41, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0af137f1-c2a3-349a-934c-db9b518e3b4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f748be531d7012c456b97f66091d86b3675c5fef <ffa6d2481bc1c87f822ecd626561484e4ee24cef"}, {"id": "13d6f9a6-b93e-3c6d-a334-cbf6ffc91eab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "419aeb96-4c16-3d92-9b07-9360454aaa03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "44a56346-10ba-386d-a82c-3f9c47d88e9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f748be531d7012c456b97f66091d86b3675c5fef <65820fc743eae322f7f94f6a64d07861211d4b21"}, {"id": "5fe0f160-dc59-3461-8a11-a901df878d65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f748be531d7012c456b97f66091d86b3675c5fef <5e38d732ec67a5b1f9a56e6c73add480c4b6030a"}, {"id": "6a31f568-a6ab-3e73-b3e6-b8043ffb27d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a97bb861-a2bf-318e-8b64-d3015709518d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.7"}, {"id": "c9517cfc-7b92-3ca9-9a5d-a1f70824daaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f748be531d7012c456b97f66091d86b3675c5fef <c28175220f808c867d5618de8ecc6dbcc815c773"}, {"id": "e615403e-6242-3656-819a-bd5be4831ae2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "e9becb5b-0905-3386-be1f-6f6808d61ea8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f748be531d7012c456b97f66091d86b3675c5fef <09c30547da2c45bb79f7d3adffc860af332c2d42"}, {"id": "ebd90203-5913-3b0c-a1b3-5ae8647ae636", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "f957533c-cc10-3bea-947f-37cfc0022631", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}], "